<refentry xml:id="function.socket-shutdown" xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook">
 <refnamediv>
  <refname>socket_shutdown</refname>
  <refpurpose>Shuts down a socket for receiving, sending, or both</refpurpose>
 </refnamediv>
 
 <refsect1 role="description">
  &reftitle.description;
  <methodsynopsis>
   <type>bool</type><methodname>socket_shutdown</methodname>
   <methodparam><type>Socket</type><parameter>socket</parameter></methodparam>
   <methodparam choice="opt"><type>int</type><parameter>mode</parameter><initializer>2</initializer></methodparam>
  </methodsynopsis>
  <para>
   The <function>socket_shutdown</function> function allows you to stop
   incoming, outgoing or all data (the default) from being sent through the
   <parameter>socket</parameter>.
  </para>
  <note>
   <para>
    The associated buffer, or buffers, may or may not be emptied.
   </para>
  </note>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1 role="parameters">
  &reftitle.parameters;
  <para>
   <variablelist>
    <varlistentry>
     <term><parameter>socket</parameter></term>
     <listitem>
      <para>
       A <classname>Socket</classname> instance created with <function>socket_create</function>.
      </para>
     </listitem>
    </varlistentry>
    <varlistentry>
     <term><parameter>mode</parameter></term>
     <listitem>
      <para>
       The value of <parameter>mode</parameter> can be one of the following:
       <table>
        <title>possible values for <parameter>mode</parameter></title>
        <tgroup cols="2">
         <tbody>
          <row>
           <entry><constant>SHUT_RD</constant> (<literal>0</literal>)</entry>
           <entry>
            Shutdown socket reading
           </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
           <entry><constant>SHUT_WR</constant> (<literal>1</literal>)</entry>
           <entry>
            Shutdown socket writing
           </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
           <entry><constant>SHUT_RDWR</constant> (<literal>2</literal>)</entry>
           <entry>
            Shutdown socket reading and writing
           </entry>
          </row>
         </tbody>
        </tgroup>
       </table>
      </para>
      <para>
       The <constant>SHUT_*</constant> constants are available as of PHP 8.5.0; the integer values can be used before.
      </para>
     </listitem>
    </varlistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </para>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1 role="returnvalues">
  &reftitle.returnvalues;
  <para>
   &return.success;
   If the socket is not connected, an <constant>E_WARNING</constant> is emitted, &false; is returned,
   and <function>socket_last_error</function> returns <constant>SOCKET_ENOTCONN</constant>.
  </para>
 </refsect1>
 <refsect1 role="errors">
  &reftitle.errors;
  <para>
   If <parameter>mode</parameter> is not <constant>SHUT_RD</constant>, <constant>SHUT_WR</constant>
   or <constant>SHUT_RDWR</constant>, a <exceptionname>ValueError</exceptionname> is thrown.
  </para>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1 role="changelog">
  &reftitle.changelog;
  <informaltable>
   <tgroup cols="2">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry>&Version;</entry>
      <entry>&Description;</entry>
     </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry>8.5.0</entry>
      <entry>
       The <constant>SHUT_RD</constant>, <constant>SHUT_WR</constant> and <constant>SHUT_RDWR</constant>
       constants have been added. A <parameter>mode</parameter> other than these values now throws a
       <exceptionname>ValueError</exceptionname>, instead of emitting an <constant>E_WARNING</constant>
       and returning &false;.
      </entry>
     </row>
     &sockets.changelog.socket-param;
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </informaltable>
 </refsect1>
 <refsect1 role="seealso">
  &reftitle.seealso;
  <para>
   <simplelist>
    <member><function>socket_close</function></member>
    <member><function>socket_connect</function></member>
    <member><function>socket_last_error</function></member>
    <member><function>stream_socket_shutdown</function></member>
   </simplelist>
  </para>
 </refsect1>
</refentry>
